----Running total & rolling total---
Running total --- aggregate all values from the begining up to current point without dropping off older data  sum(Sales) over(order by month)  rows between unbounded precedings and current row
Rolling total ---- aggregates all the values within the fixed time window (like 30 days) as new data ios added , the oldest dtaa point will be dropped.  sum(Sales) over(order by month rows between 2 precedings and current row)


---Moving average ---
calculate moving average of sales for each product over time

select orderid,productid,orderdate, sales,avg(Sales) over(partition by productid) avgbyproduct,avg(sales) over(partition by productid order by orderdate) Movingavg from sales.orders

---Moving average ---
calculate moving average of sales for each product over time

select orderid,productid,orderdate, sales,avg(Sales) over(partition by productid) avgbyproduct,avg(sales) over(partition by productid order by orderdate) Movingavg,avg(Sales) over(partition by productid order by orderdate rows between current row and 1 following) Rollingavg from sales.orders


---overall toatal and total per groups---

overall total : overview of entire data sum(Sales) over()
Total per groups : compare categories sum(Sales) over(partition by product)
running total : progress over time   sum(Sales) over(order by month)
Rolling total : progress over time within specific window  sum(Sales) over(order by month rows 2 precedings)





All-in-One Example
SELECT
    Product,
    Sales,
    COUNT(*) OVER(PARTITION BY Product)  AS Product_Count,
    SUM(Sales) OVER(PARTITION BY Product)  AS Total_Sales,
    AVG(Sales) OVER(PARTITION BY Product)  AS Avg_Sales,
    MIN(Sales) OVER(PARTITION BY Product)  AS Min_Sales,
    MAX(Sales) OVER(PARTITION BY Product)  AS Max_Sales
FROM Sales;



Quick Reference
Goal	Window function
Overall total	SUM(Sales) OVER()
Total per group	SUM(Sales) OVER(PARTITION BY product)
Running total	SUM(Sales) OVER(ORDER BY month)
Rolling total	SUM(Sales) OVER(ORDER BY month ROWS 2 PRECEDING)
Count incl. NULLs	COUNT(*) OVER(...)
Count excl. NULLs	COUNT(column) OVER(...)
Duplicates check	COUNT(*) OVER(PARTITION BY pk) > 1
Above-average rows	WHERE sales > AVG(sales) OVER() (via subquery)
Handle NULLs in avg	AVG(COALESCE(sales, 0)) OVER(...)







